@startuml State Machine - WebSocket Client
!theme plain
title WebSocket Client State Machine — Dashboard Side

[*] --> DISCONNECTED

DISCONNECTED --> CONNECTING : user opens dashboard
DISCONNECTED : entry / show "Disconnected" badge

CONNECTING --> CONNECTED : connection accepted
CONNECTING --> WAIT_RETRY : connection refused\nor timeout
CONNECTING : entry / ws = new WebSocket(url + "?token=...")

CONNECTED --> RECEIVING_CONFIG : server sends signal_config
CONNECTED : entry / show "Connected" badge

RECEIVING_CONFIG --> STREAMING : all configs received\n+ snapshot received
RECEIVING_CONFIG : do / store signal metadata

STREAMING --> STREAMING : signal_update received\n/ update UI widgets
STREAMING --> ALARM : alarm message received
STREAMING --> DISCONNECTED : connection closed\nby server
STREAMING --> WAIT_RETRY : no heartbeat\nfor 15 seconds
STREAMING : entry / show "Live" badge
STREAMING : do / update gauges, charts, table

ALARM --> STREAMING : alarm handled\n/ show alarm bar
ALARM : entry / show alarm notification\n/ play alert sound

WAIT_RETRY --> CONNECTING : backoff timer expired\n(1s, 2s, 4s, ..., 30s max)
WAIT_RETRY --> DISCONNECTED : max_retries exceeded
WAIT_RETRY : entry / increment retry_count\n/ calculate backoff delay
WAIT_RETRY : do / show "Reconnecting..." badge

note right of WAIT_RETRY
    Exponential backoff:
    delay = min(2^retry * 1s, 30s)
end note

@enduml
